]},{"id":"401892723000000900","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":1,"text":"Matvei Gridin Snap Shot Above Crossbar","type":{"id":"507","text":"Missed","abbreviation":"shot-missed"},"clock":{"displayValue":"3:10"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"3"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5216897","displayName":"Matvei Gridin","shortName":"M. Gridin"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"3151137","displayName":"Ville Husso","shortName":"V. Husso"}}]},{"id":"401892723000000080","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":1,"text":"Puck in Crowd","type":{"id":"516","text":"Stoppage","abbreviation":"stoppage"},"clock":{"displayValue":"3:12"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"}},{"id":"401892723000000910","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":1,"text":"Mikael Granlund faceoff won against Joel Farabee","type":{"id":"502","text":"Face Off","abbreviation":"faceoff"},"clock":{"displayValue":"3:12"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"25"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5831","displayName":"Mikael Granlund","shortName":"M. Granlund"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"4352750","displayName":"Joel Farabee","shortName":"J. Farabee"}}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1842","fullName":"Honda Center","address":{"city":"Anaheim","state":"CA","zipCode":"92899","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1842.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":15686,"officials":[{"fullName":"Jonny Murray","displayName":"Jonny Murray","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Carter Sandlak","displayName":"Carter Sandlak","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Tom Chmielewski","displayName":"Tom Chmielewski","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Onni Hautamaki","displayName":"Onni Hautamaki","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Cutter Gauthier extends goal streak to 9 games, leading Ducks past Flames 6-1","description":"— Cutter Gauthier extended the NHL's longest goals streak in 29 years to nine games, and Beckett Sennecke had two goals and an assist in the Anaheim Ducks' 6-1 victory over the Calgary Flames on Sunday night.","story":"ANAHEIM, Calif. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080145/cutter-gauthier\">Cutter Gauthier</a> extended the NHL's longest goals streak in 29 years to nine games, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5216858/beckett-sennecke\">Beckett Sennecke</a> had two goals and an assist in the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/ana/anaheim-ducks\">Anaheim Ducks</a>' 6-1 victory over the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/cgy/calgary-flames\">Calgary Flames</a> on Sunday night.\n\n\r\n              Captain <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5831/mikael-granlund\">Mikael Granlund</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4895214/jeff-malott\">Jeff Malott</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4996085/tim-washe\">Tim Washe</a> also scored and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3151137/ville-husso\">Ville Husso</a> made 20 saves for the Ducks, who rebounded smartly <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/islanders-ducks-score-874943ec3d06f487cd247c62d4d4e47f\">from consecutive unimpressive losses</a> for their sixth victory in eight games overall.\n\n\r\n              Gauthier added to his streak in style during the first period, ripping a wrist shot past <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4319911/devin-cooley\">Devin Cooley</a> from the far side of the faceoff circle. Gauthier has 16 goals during this binge and 18 on the season, second-most in the NHL behind Edmonton’s <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114727/leon-draisaitl\">Leon Draisaitl</a>.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3797/mikael-backlund\">Mikael Backlund</a> scored in the third period and Cooley stopped 28 shots for the Flames, who have lost four of six. Calgary <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/kings-flames-score-2590c6fad96690a9d6705e810aeab17f\">beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/la/los-angeles-kings\">Los Angeles Kings</a> one night earlier</a> to open a three-game California trip.\n\n\r\n              Gauthier's goals streak is the second-longest in Ducks history and the longest since Teemu Selanne scored in 11 straight for Anaheim in 1997. He's tied for the sixth-longest streak in the NHL since 1991, and he's only the fifth player under the age of 23 to score a goal in nine straight games, joining Selanne, Wayne Gretzky, Mike Bossy and Babe Dye.\n\n\r\n              Gauthier’s 11-game points streak also is the longest of his career.\n\n\r\n              Malott scored 1:16 after the opening faceoff, swatting in a rebound from the slot.\n\n\r\n              Backlund ended the Ducks' bid for their first shutout win in over two years on a breakaway early in the third, but Sennecke blasted a one-timer just 25 seconds later. Shortly after Sennecke scored an empty-netter to secure his third multi-goal game of the season, Granlund scored with Cooley back in net.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5188523/ian-moore\">Ian Moore</a> had an assist in his season debut for Anaheim after incurring a high ankle sprain on the opening day of training camp.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Flames: At San Jose on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Ducks: At St. Louis on Tuesday night to open a four-game trip.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-16T03:41:34Z"}}